---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Card from "../components/Card.astro";
---

<Base title="Open questions — Party Dungeon" current="/open/">
  <header>
    <div class="kicker">Still undecided</div>
    <h1>What we don't know yet.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Questions that change what gets built, listed roughly in the order they
      need answers.
    </p>
  </header>

  <Section title="Still open">
    <Card>
      <ul class="plain">
        <li>
          <b>Session shape.</b> How long is a run, and what does a full session
          look like from login to logoff?
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Who's in the map with you.</b> Allies against the map, or a rival
          party competing in it?
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Why visit an open dungeon.</b> Look, fight, trade, steal &mdash;
          which one is the first one?
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Combat feel.</b> Real-time action with cooldowns, or something
          slower?
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Netcode shape.</b> Client-server, host-authoritative, or
          peer-to-peer &mdash; and how many players at once?
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Progression.</b> What carries between runs besides the dungeon
          itself?
        </li>
      </ul>
    </Card>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Open thread">
    <Card>
      <p class="quote">
        "The user will have a personal dungeon that can be opened to the
        public."
      </p>
      <p>
        That sentence puts a door on the base. It means the dungeon is a
        <strong>venue</strong> with traffic, not a menu with upgrades &mdash;
        and it's the piece most likely to define what this game is.
      </p>
    </Card>
  </Section>
</Base>
